sequenceDiagram
  %% Future design (Nick 2026-11-02): today's half-built smoke is removed; build this later as a feature. Target design proposal: smoke as steps of the automatic-deploy fire (instance.auto_deploy), repo-owned Pest tests in GitHub Actions (Recall production-smoke-repo-owned-github-actions). Replaces instance.smoke plus its control, failure, rollback, redeploy and repair endpoints. docs/reference/deployments.md#production-smoke.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:auto-deploy · Production smoke
  %% kind: instance.smoke
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=tests tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as app-prod Node<br/>Node 12 over ssh
  participant GH as GitHub Actions<br/>smoke workflow
  Note over SW: Fire found green commit<br/>auto-deploy-42 · a1b2c3d
  %%> When:
  %%> - an automatic-deploy fire of Instance 42 found a newer green commit
  %%> - only when the Project opts in to smoke
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the smoke workflow file and ref, the Route URL `https://shop.com`
  %%> - a vault key name for a GitHub token with Actions write; the Gateway keeps it fresh
  SW->>N: Deploy the pinned commit<br/>deploy-42 · prepare … check
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the same steps as `instance:deploy`; the previous release stays on the Node
  SW->>GH: Start the smoke tests<br/>workflow_dispatch · commit, URL
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts the repository's smoke workflow against `https://shop.com`
  %%> - sends the commit and the deployment id; nothing else
  %%> What runs there:
  %%> - the repository's own Pest browser tests, owned by the repository
  loop every 15 s, up to 10 min
    SW->>GH: Read run and JUnit<br/>run status · smoke.xml artifact
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - finds the run by its name `Smoke <deployment> <commit>`
    %%> - when it ends, reads the JUnit report from its artifact
  end
  alt tests passed
    SW-->>GW: Fire ended<br/>deployed · smoke passed
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the release stays live
    Note over GW: Record deployment<br/>smoke passed · run link
    %%> Result:
    %%> - history row with the smoke result and the GitHub run link
  else tests failed
    SW->>N: Roll back to previous<br/>switch current · reload
    %%> When:
    %%> - only when JUnit has real failures or errors; a red run without them is "unknown"
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - switches `current` back to the previous release; the same steps as `instance:rollback`
    SW-->>GW: Fire ended<br/>smoke failed · rolled back
    Note over GW: Block commit, pause, alert<br/>failed tests · run link
    %%> Result:
    %%> - commit `a1b2c3d` is blocked; it never deploys automatically again
    %%> - auto-deploy pauses until you enable it again
    %%> - an alert names the failed tests and links the run
    %%> Optional:
    %%> - the Gateway creates a repair task with the failure, when tasks are on
  else no clear result
    SW-->>GW: Fire ended<br/>smoke unknown
    %%> When:
    %%> - no run found, no JUnit, or 10 minutes passed
    Note over GW: Keep release, pause, alert<br/>smoke unknown
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the release stays live; Orbit never rolls back without proof of failure
    %%> - auto-deploy pauses, and an alert asks you to check
  end
